WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.460
- You asked me to watch
South Park medical scenes.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.630
I said, "Get this
comment to 10,000 likes."

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.843
And you did it, so let's watch it.

00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:06.676
(claps once)

00:00:06.676 --> 00:00:07.509
Bewoop!

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:09.010
- No shots! No shots!

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.240
- Eric, you have to be a big boy.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.060
- Big boys get a toy from the toy chest.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.780
- See the doctor's getting it wrong.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.130
You have to give the toy
first, earn the trust,

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.643
then have the shot be injected.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:21.057
(hip hop beat)

00:00:21.057 --> 00:00:22.270
(Eric screams)

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.960
- And don't let them visualize the shot.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.020
It's scary to look at that.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.050
Keep it on the side, keep
it out of their vision

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.080
and have them look elsewhere.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.876
(Eric screams)

00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:33.000
(glass breaking)

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.212
This is like a scene
out of a horror movie.

00:00:34.212 --> 00:00:35.262
(Eric screams)

00:00:35.262 --> 00:00:39.083
(Eric squeals like a pig)

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:40.720
(papers rustling)

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.240
- I'm sorry, but I have a
lot of other patients to see.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.930
We'll just have to try again next week.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.400
- Come on, Eric, we're going home.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.670
- We're going home? You promise?

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.503
- Let's go, get in the car!

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.790
- Why is he still nude?

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.440
And no, you shouldn't leave the office

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.740
just because the child
doesn't want the vaccinations.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.600
Vaccinations are an incredibly
important part of growing up

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.010
and growing up healthy and safe.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.170
So yes, please get your
children vaccinated

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.970
and don't let them walk around nude

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.160
in a medical office like that.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.090
That's just strange.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:08.923
- What have we got?

00:01:08.923 --> 00:01:10.588
- Not sure, looks like
a possible code 5-6.

00:01:10.588 --> 00:01:12.350
- Kitty, shut up Kitty.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.827
- I'm not sure if he has pink eye?

00:01:13.827 --> 00:01:17.230
Or is that like a
subconjunctival hemorrhage?

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:19.060
Which is actually really
benign in most cases.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.010
The way that the paramedics
brought him in there,

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:21.843
pretty legit,

00:01:21.843 --> 00:01:24.280
minus the fact they said he's code 5-6.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.150
That is not medical jargon.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.030
I'm sorry, South Park.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:29.940
- Get me 50 ccs of ketamine STAT!

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.744
And get something for the kid, too.

00:01:31.744 --> 00:01:33.122
(Dr. Mike laughs hysterically)

00:01:33.122 --> 00:01:34.920
- Oh that was actually really funny!

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.480
Ketamine is a tranquilizer.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.640
It's technically a, it started
as an animal tranquilizer,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.497
and now we've actually
found some medical uses

00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:43.080
for it in humans.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.340
I actually have a whole video on this

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.930
talking about how ketamine infusions

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.750
are being used for
treatment-resistant depression.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.793
Link down below.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.420
- His EKG is showing

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.560
that he's like a failing
stock market stock.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.393
What is happening?

00:01:55.393 --> 00:01:57.310
And his EKG next to his bedside,

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.240
I don't even know what that is.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.280
That's not a medical rhythm.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.743
- I'm afraid he's running out of time.

00:02:01.743 --> 00:02:03.300
(medical instrument beeps)

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.720
- Why? What's wrong with him?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.309
- It's his time. It's running out.

00:02:07.309 --> 00:02:08.142
(Dr. Mike laughs)

00:02:08.142 --> 00:02:09.320
- Well, what does he need?

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.780
- He needs to have more time.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.613
- Oh my God.

00:02:11.613 --> 00:02:12.800
This reminds me of the movie Out of Time

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:13.800
with Justin Timberlake.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.270
That was such a good movie.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.430
Where like, time is money.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.710
Literally time was money,
because time is money.

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:20.190
But money is not time.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.290
And then if you have enough time,

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.160
you run out of money.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:23.993
I'm lost.

00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:29.074
(Eric screams)

00:02:29.074 --> 00:02:30.399
- Poopsy-kins?

00:02:30.399 --> 00:02:32.890
(panicked yelling)

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:33.723
- Sweety, what is ?

00:02:33.723 --> 00:02:35.340
(Mother screams)

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.690
- I'm ginger!

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.260
- Oh my God! Eric!

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.750
- Help me!

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.293
Help me!

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.100
- Is this a medical condition?

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.090
- Well, all his vital
signs are still normal.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.110
From his outward appearance

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:50.440
I would say he has the standard
skin pigment deficiency.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.540
- You mean?

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.373
- Yes.

00:02:52.373 --> 00:02:54.968
I'm afraid that your son is
suffering from ginger-vitis.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.868
- But how could I become a ginger now?

00:02:58.253 --> 00:03:00.050
- It's a play on gingivitis,

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.640
which is inflammation of the gums.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:03.620
But there's actually been
a lot of misconceptions

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.800
about folks who have red hair.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.250
Specifically in the medical community.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.130
There was a thought

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.390
where they tested
individuals with red hair

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.530
and they found that they
required more anesthesia

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.460
than other patients.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.900
However, once we've expanded the research

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:15.810
to have more patients,

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.640
we found that to be completely untrue.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.500
So there's a lot of myths
about folks with red hair,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.710
of them being emotional,

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.560
needing more medication for anesthesia.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:24.960
None of this is proven.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.010
What's the saying, Sam?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.383
When something is like,

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.110
like, legend has it.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:31.943
- [Sam] Urban legend.

00:03:31.943 --> 00:03:32.870
- It's an urban legend.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.780
- You need to understand there is no cure.

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.410
Your son will be ginger his whole life.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.510
- For individuals who
do have very light skin,

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.700
pale skin like this,

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.890
and for individuals who have

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:43.320
a high number of moles on their body,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.940
you actually are at a higher risk

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.960
for developing skin cancers and sunburns.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.350
So please, shade is your friend.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.210
SPF is your next best friend.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.620
- You're gonna have to take
certain precautions now.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:56.330
It's very important that you
keep Eric out of the sun.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:58.100
- Oh. My favorite part about that

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.410
is not that he confirmed my diagnosis

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.500
of being careful with the sun,

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.333
But the fact that

00:04:02.333 --> 00:04:04.710
he went to the University
of the Mountains.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.340
- I don't know what to do, Sharon.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.080
They want to have him go into surgery

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.530
but that's so dangerous.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.120
- Sheila, have you tried
holistic natural medicines?

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:12.990
They work wonders.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.220
I read all about it in People.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.720
- Really? In People?

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.360
- There's a brand new shop in town

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.930
that sells holistic medicines
and all natural foods.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:23.530
It's run by this fascinating
woman named Misinformation.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.940
- That reminds me of
Goop. I don't know why.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.730
I'm getting Gwyneth
Paltrow vibes from this.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.750
Although I have one major correction here.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.240
Holistic does not mean frou-frou..

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.600
Holistic does not mean naturopathic.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.750
Holistic means whole person.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.300
In fact, when I treat my patients

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.050
I treat them with holistic care.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.660
I give them medical care.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:44.140
Sometimes it's a natural
lifestyle-based approach.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.040
Sometimes it's a
medication-based approach.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:46.900
Sometimes it's surgical.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.970
If a person comes in with a heart attack

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.830
I don't just say, "Oh, that's
the heart attack patient."

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.810
No, we think about what's
going on in their lives.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:53.900
How can they eat better?

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.480
What can they do to start exercising

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.580
once it's safe to do so?

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.930
What medication should they be on?

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.450
Can they afford these medications?

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.970
What's going on in their personal life?

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.760
Like, if you think about
all these variables,

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.450
you're going to have a better chance

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.670
of getting that person healthier.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.260
Wow. I just went on a
rant about South Park.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.440
- You see the reasons our bodies
fail is because of toxins.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:12.320
- Toxins?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.640
- All the horrible food we eat.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.830
The sodas and meats
are filled with toxins.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.490
And the only way for us to get better

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.780
is to flush those toxins
out of our system.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:22.560
- And I wonder how we get rid of toxins?

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.900
We have body parts that
actually do it for us!

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.350
Surprise, surprise!

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:27.330
The lungs do it.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.200
The kidneys do it.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.180
The liver does it.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.450
It gets out those evil toxins.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:33.500
You know what's funny about
the trigger word toxins?

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.920
You know you can scare people

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.590
into buying something
that they don't need.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.750
You don't even know what a
toxin is when you say it.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.700
Like water is an essential
component of my being.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.970
But if I have too much of it

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.070
I can actually dilute my
body's electrolytes so much so

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:47.470
that I can kill myself, essentially,

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:48.550
by drinking too much water.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.250
The toxicity of a substance

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.580
can really only be dictated by the dose.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.760
So don't let people scare you

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.073
when they throw around words like that.

00:05:55.073 --> 00:05:57.070
- Mrs. Baflowsky would
like to give your son

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.580
herbs that focus on the kidney.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.820
I have these excellent herbs

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.483
from local Native Americans.

00:06:01.483 --> 00:06:02.860
- Ooh, Native Americans.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.020
Now they know how to heal
the body spiritually.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.930
- Ho did it go from holistic care

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.820
to spiritual care in one herbal second?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:10.730
- Hi, Doctor.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:11.870
- What can I do for you?

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.510
Well, it's my friend, Kyle.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.260
I think he's really, really sick.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.240
- He is really, really sick, Stanley.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.583
Your little friend Kyle
needs a kidney transplant

00:06:19.583 --> 00:06:22.450
or it is very possible that he will die.

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.150
- Why does Kyle need a kidney transplant?

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.760
That's an aggressive procedure.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.490
Like, he needs to have something

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.980
tremendously wrong with
both of his kidneys

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.050
to need and warrant a kidney transplant.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.760
I need to know the indication for this.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.990
I'm taking this too seriously.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.620
- There's only one person in South park

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.370
with the same blood type as Kyle.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.203
- Who?

00:06:40.347 --> 00:06:41.400
(Dr. Mike laughs)

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.550
- Kyle's in trouble, Cartman.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.530
I can see him getting
worse right before my eyes.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.980
There might be a way that
you can save his life.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:47.813
- Uh huh?

00:06:47.813 --> 00:06:49.560
- What Kyle really needs is a new kidney.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.446
Will you donate one of
your kidneys to Kyle?

00:06:51.446 --> 00:06:53.715
♪ No, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no! ♪

00:06:53.715 --> 00:06:55.006
- You only need one, fatboy!

00:06:55.006 --> 00:06:56.654
♪ No, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no! ♪

00:06:56.654 --> 00:06:57.487
- Dude, one of your
friends is going to die.

00:06:57.487 --> 00:06:58.630
Don't you see how serious this is?

00:06:58.630 --> 00:06:59.463
- For the record:

00:06:59.463 --> 00:07:00.400
Humans have two kidneys,

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.820
and only need one kidney to live.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.470
In fact there are some individuals

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:05.840
who actually have only
one kidney and do great,

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.440
but if something happens to their kidney,

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.790
like it could happen to anybody else

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:09.650
to both of their kidneys,

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:10.760
they don't have a backup.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:12.030
So it becomes more dangerous.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.350
- Free-range Aspirin!

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.276
- All natural cell phones!

00:07:14.276 --> 00:07:16.020
- Free-range Aspirin.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.045
It just hit me what that is.

00:07:18.045 --> 00:07:19.590
(Dr. Mike laughs loudly)

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.230
I dunno why I found that so funny.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.300
- Oh, hi, Stanley.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.890
Look, I'm buying you some
more all natural toothpaste.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.130
- You mean the stuff
that tastes like (bleep)

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.050
and doesn't fight cavities?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.080
- That's right.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.570
- Look, um, I know that you all think

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:31.670
the earth and its natural
healing powers can cure Kyle,

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.690
but the doctor at the
hospital told me it can't.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:35.660
- Well of course the doctor told you that

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.550
because he wants to make money.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.010
Holistic medicine is about nature!

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.160
- And it's free!

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.260
Yet she's standing in
front of her cash register

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.927
asking for a deposit!

00:07:44.927 --> 00:07:46.300
- $233

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.390
- For $233!

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.463
- Okay, here we go.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.520
Okay. Well, here goes nothing.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:53.600
Help me pull his pajamas up.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:54.433
- Okay.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.130
I think this goes without being said.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.821
Don't get a wood saw

00:08:02.821 --> 00:08:06.600
and operate on your friend
who needs a kidney transplant

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.180
at home.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.460
I don't know who needs to hear that,

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.264
but I'm just putting out
there into the ether.

00:08:12.264 --> 00:08:13.665
(children shouting "Hooray!")

00:08:13.665 --> 00:08:15.724
(alarm bell ringing)

00:08:15.724 --> 00:08:18.457
(Eric yawns)

00:08:18.457 --> 00:08:19.540
(Eric yells)

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.140
- That son of a (bleep)!

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.583
- Who just wakes up from
a nap missing a kidney?

00:08:23.583 --> 00:08:25.080
- Give me back my kidney!

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.500
- Dude, please, Kyle needs it.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.670
- It's mine!

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:29.150
Not yours, mine!

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.470
Give it back right now or
there's going to be hell to pay!

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:32.910
- Alright, alright, here.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:34.340
- That actually looks like a good kidney!

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.320
Wow! Well done, South Park.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.935
- Why hello there, Eric.

00:08:37.935 --> 00:08:39.290
(kidney hits table)

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.390
- You see that? That's mine!

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:44.065
Stan took my kidney and
I need to put it back in.

00:08:44.065 --> 00:08:44.898
Please.

00:08:44.898 --> 00:08:46.550
- Oh, I see.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:48.360
Are you sure now that it's already out

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.710
you don't want to just let
your friend Kyle have it?

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.740
- No, because it doesn't belong to Kyle,

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.005
it belongs to me.

00:08:54.005 --> 00:08:54.838
It's mine!

00:08:54.838 --> 00:08:57.050
- Well, alright then, we'll
get you prepped for surgery.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.912
If you'll just sign this release.

00:08:58.912 --> 00:08:59.745
- Thank you.

00:08:59.745 --> 00:09:00.578
(pen scribbles)

00:09:00.578 --> 00:09:01.411
- How are you feeling, Bobby?

00:09:01.411 --> 00:09:02.490
- Better, thanks.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:03.630
- You look a lot better.

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.850
- Yeah, it looks like Western
medicine really did the trick.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.828
- Kyle's all better,
Cartman, thanks to you!

00:09:07.828 --> 00:09:08.661
- Huh?

00:09:08.661 --> 00:09:09.494
- It was all a trick.

00:09:09.494 --> 00:09:10.327
Your mama did the kidney blocker

00:09:10.327 --> 00:09:11.180
and then we put ketchup in your bed

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.530
so you'd think we took your kidney.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:13.910
- Yes, but it was all just a trick

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.880
to get you to come in
and sign this release.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:16.810
- What's worse:

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:19.560
Nurse Jackie in the
episode that I watched?

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.160
If she forged his Oregon donor certificate

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.400
on the back of his license, that's crazy.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:27.590
Or them tricking Cartman
to sign away his own kidney

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:30.200
by thinking he's actually
getting his kidney put back in?

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:33.140
What is happening with
the ethics on these shows?

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:34.410
I also watch Simpsons

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:36.310
and review the medical
scenes in that bad boy.

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.240
Check it out and enjoy the laugh.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.313
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:43.788
I just want to say bewoop
one more time, Bewoop!

00:09:43.788 --> 00:09:46.788
(slow hip hop beat)

